/target

# `gen/` is `cargo tauri android init`'s output and almost all of it is
# regenerated on demand: the wrapper, `buildSrc`, the res tree, the launcher
# icons, wry's `generated/` sources, `tauri.settings.gradle`. Ignoring the lot
# is right for those.
#
# **What is under `gen/android` and NOT generated is ours.** Two whole modules
# (`edet-keystore`, `edet-background`), the `settings.gradle` that wires them
# into the app, `app/build.gradle.kts`, and `MainActivity.kt` — which carries
# the WebView re-resume that is the whole of background mode on Android.
# `tauri android init` creates none of them, so nothing regenerates them on a
# checkout that lacks them: they travel with the tree or they are gone.
#
# They were tracked with `git add -f` under a blanket `/gen`, and a file that
# is tracked-but-ignored travels only through git history. A tree imported any
# other way — a tarball unpacked into a fresh `git init && git add -A`, a
# mirror populated from an export — silently drops every one of them, and what
# that looks like is `:edet-keystore` resolving to a directory with no build
# file: Gradle makes an empty project of it and the custody workflow fails
# with "Cannot locate tasks that match
# ':edet-keystore:assembleDebugAndroidTest'", while `regeneration` passes
# vacuously, because `git status --porcelain src-tauri/gen` is empty when the
# files are untracked AND ignored.
#
# So the ignore is a whitelist, and it is written along the ownership boundary
# rather than file by file: an `edet-*` module is ours whole, and Kotlin under
# the app that is not in wry's `generated/` is ours. A file added to either —
# or a third `edet-*` module — is carried with no edit here.
/gen/**
# Directories back in, or git stops at `gen/android` and never reaches a file.
!/gen/**/

# Ours whole. The prefix is the boundary: tauri's own modules are `app` and
# `buildSrc`, and every module we add is `edet-something`.
!/gen/android/edet-*/**

# The app project is tauri's, less the two build scripts that wire our modules
# in and the Kotlin we write in it. `generated/` is wry's, written on every
# Android build of the app.
!/gen/android/settings.gradle
!/gen/android/app/build.gradle.kts
!/gen/android/app/src/main/java/**
/gen/android/app/src/main/java/org/edet/client/generated/

# Re-including every directory walks Gradle's output as well, which is tens of
# thousands of files and is not a thing to walk. Back out, after the negations
# above so these win — they are output under our modules too.
/gen/**/build/
/gen/**/.gradle/
/gen/**/.kotlin/
/gen/**/.cxx/
